Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 09:30:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03807/11362] [outer-loop] Lever #4 (mechanic-template): the
 PERCEPTION wall unifying all 5 multi-level lever nulls

Built the align_to_goal_offset template (grid-grounded detector + parameterized is_level_complete + smooth
goal_energy descent gradient; verified on synthetic data; build on branch outer-loop/multiwin-goal dd2140c1c).
On REAL grids it exposes a deeper, unifying obstacle: the logical grid does NOT expose the structural objects
the win conditions are defined over. lp85's rotation RECOLORS the whole board (no stable object identity);
r11l has no stationary goal anchor; tu93's win is a trail not a clean player->goal; bp35/g50t aren't even
explorer-reachable. ARC win conditions are object-relational (internal sprite tags); per-game adapters read
that internal state (non-generalizing); plan_in_model + any GENERIC grid-grounded goal (template OR
LLM-induced) operate on pixels that lose object identity.

This UNIFIES the 5 nulls (#1 value-biased, #2 multi-positive, conductor A1 hierarchical-subgoal, A2 PoE-World,
#4 template): the L1->L2 wall is a PERCEPTION / object-identity problem (recover stable objects from the
rendered grid), not goal-induction/search/planning -- matching the project's prior 'perception is the binding
constraint' finding. Recommendation: redirect to a generic object-perception layer (segment frames into
persistent objects, track by shape/motion not color); the template's goal_energy is ready to consume it.
Bigger build than a lever; the honest next direction (or first-win breadth for 6/30 while perception is a
longer-horizon investment). verifier_is_oracle:true (execution-grounded, not a moat).

